    "is_free": false,
    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Welcome to the office of W.A. Throckmorton.</strong><br>You\u2019re the custodian at a university where the faculty have more credentials than sense.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > You\u2019re sent to fetch an absent-minded professor who is late for a faculty meeting, but thanks to his  security device, you\u2019re now trapped inside his office, and he's trapped somewhere far stranger! </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The radio is the only link between you and the world he\u2019s lost in.  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Explore the professor\u2019s office, shift time, and uncover hidden connections between objects and stories. Solve layered puzzles that bend logic and memory. Your choices shape what unfolds.</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Welcome to the office of W.A. Throckmorton.</strong><br>You\u2019re the custodian at a university where the faculty have more credentials than sense.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > You\u2019re sent to fetch an absent-minded professor who is late for a faculty meeting, but thanks to his  security device, you\u2019re now trapped inside his office, and he's trapped somewhere far stranger! </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The radio is the only link between you and the world he\u2019s lost in.  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Explore the professor\u2019s office, shift time, and uncover hidden connections between objects and stories. Solve layered puzzles that bend logic and memory. Your choices shape what unfolds.</p>",
    "short_description": "The Radio is a narrative-driven escape room mystery where you must free a trapped professor from his own choose-your-own adventure radio drama. Use objects in his office like books, pictures, curious devices, and even a time-bending clock, to solve puzzles that bridge the gap between two realities.",
